WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.610
Class 3-B?

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.760
Ms. Kuroi!

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:05.920
Yeah, yeah...

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:36.090
You've been messing around there for a while...

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.170
...but can you even tell?

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:39.010
Aren't they all the same?

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:41.180
Isn't it common sense to do this?

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:43.890
Otherwise, you could spend all the money
in the world and never get what you want.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:46.970
Your common sense has very little practical application.

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:50.230
At the very least, normal people wouldn't do it.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:54.770
It isn't just about figures...

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:57.480
Some people are after the cards.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.740
How can you distinguish between cards?

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:00.900
Don't they all weigh the same?

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:04.410
There have been many legends and rumors about this.

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:06.080
Like where to find good cards...

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.870
Or special marks or patterns to look for.

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:13.420
By the way, I can usually get the special cards I want.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:14.880
There's a pattern to it...

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.090
...if the box was just opened.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:18.300
<i>That's pretty insane if you think about it...</i>

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.960
<i>...but I really don't feel like praising her!</i>

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.590
If people know these things...

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:23.890
...don't the good ones get taken in no time?

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:25.550
That's true...

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.140
If you live in an area with experts...

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:31.180
...rare cards and secret figures are gone in a flash.

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:34.850
When I go to a shop and see all these gaps in a box...

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:36.810
...I'm left in despair.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:40.070
But then I end up falling for that faint glimmer of hope.

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:41.030
It's such a problem.

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:42.990
You definitely have a problematic nature.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.700
I heard some collectors...

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:47.490
...go out and buy a whole bunch at once?

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:48.740
Yeah.

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:49.790
Some do.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:52.160
It's faster to complete a set if you buy a bunch at once...

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:54.500
...and it's easier to read distribution patterns that way.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:54.960
Oh, really.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:58.840
Well, they call it the adult purchasing
method since it's a strain on your budget.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:00.460
Gotta work part-time to support it.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:01.800
Adult purchasing method, huh...

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:03.550
They might call it an adult method...

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.510
...but they sure act immature.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.220
It signifies a really possessive nature...

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.100
...or selfish behaviour.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:12.100
Maybe the young adult purchasing method would be better.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:16.310
Am I the only one who thinks that
spending the effort on something else...

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:17.440
...would be more meaningful?

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:19.610
These days...

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:23.950
Akihabara gets a lot more media attention.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:26.410
And they're obnoxious about it.

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:27.780
They can do stories if they want...

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.870
...but I have yet to see anything based on factual evidence.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:33.120
Well, they probably exaggerate some stuff...

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.660
...but isn't that because of their audience?

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.330
But that doesn't explain how TV shows and songs...

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:40.460
...which were big in geek culture first become popular.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:44.760
News programs and variety shows
use anime and game music all the time.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:45.510
Well...

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:49.390
Maybe that's because normal people wouldn't recognize it?

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:51.060
Speaking of geeks...

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:52.470
Male geeks...

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:55.940
...are always talking about how they want a
geek with the same interests for a girlfriend...

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:57.770
...on forums and stuff.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:02.320
But you never hear a female geek
wanting to go out with another geek.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:03.570
I wonder why.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:06.610
Maybe girls are more susceptible to the charms of 2-D.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:09.700
Maybe they're worried about the future?

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:12.370
I'm sure most of those are working though...

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:13.740
And like, don't ask me this stuff.

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:23.460
They showed up as soon as it got hot.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:25.880
Can't stand how they're noisy and quick to escape.

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:26.630
And they're dirty.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:28.590
They say that Musashi Miyamoto...

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:31.180
...could catch flies using chopsticks.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:32.010
For real?!

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:35.640
I can't believe he was willing to
touch those things with eating utensils.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:36.560
Makes me sick.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:37.520
That's your concern?

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:38.600
Well, I know what you mean...

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:45.780
Abeshi!

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:48.820
Wow!

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:51.030
I could never smack a mosquito.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:52.450
Why's that?

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:55.910
It'd be all gross when blood got
over your hand when you crushed it.

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.290
That's true...

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:58.580
That's my blood.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:02.210
But what if a mosquito lands on your arm?

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:05.340
I'm go, "Shoo! Shoo!"

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:06.630
Or I blow on it.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:10.300
Did you know?

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.600
If you clench your arm when a mosquito lands on it...

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.060
...it can't pull its stinger out.

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:14.720
No way!

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:15.850
Just watch.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:21.940
You are already dead.

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:23.770
You've already been bitten.

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:25.360
If you clench even harder...

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:26.820
...the mosquito will explode.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:28.280
Stop! Stop!

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:29.450
It itches!

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:29.860
<i>Should have just smacked it in the first place.</i>

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:32.160
Itches so much!

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:35.950
Are you going overseas again this summer, Miyuki-san?

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:36.540
No.

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:38.290
Not this year.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:38.910
However...

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:41.170
...we will probably visit relatives in the country.

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:46.420
I also often go to the summer festival
with the neighbour's daughter from Ryouou.

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:48.840
She's like a younger sister.

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:53.140
So you're going to a summer festival, Iwasaki-san.

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:55.260
You'd probably look great in a yukata.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:56.010
Not at all...

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:59.560
<i>I know that you're complimenting me...</i>

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:01.770
<i>...but for some reason, I can't appreciate it.</i>

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:03.770
<i>It's like you're saying I don't have any...</i>

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:08.860
Be right there...

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:10.400
Yo...

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:11.360
Morning...

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:12.490
You just woke up?!

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:13.320
What a slob.

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:14.370
Well...

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:17.240
Something's really been bothering me lately.

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:17.700
What?

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:19.910
Like, did my alarm clock ring?

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:23.080
Or like, did somebody else turn it off?

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:25.420
I know what you mean!

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:27.800
When you look, the switch's off.

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:30.090
But then again, it gets hot in the afternoon...

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:31.920
...so I can't really keep sleeping.

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:33.510
We're well into the afternoon.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:34.890
Kona-chan.

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:35.930
It's morning.

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:37.180
Wake up.

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:38.720
Izumi-kun.

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:40.270
Let's eat lunch together.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:44.350
I thought I might go home with you, Konata-kun.

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:45.560
Hey, Konata.

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:48.440
Why are the main characters in those games...

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:50.320
...so unconditionally popular?

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:51.190
Beats me...

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:53.990
Maybe 'cause it wouldn't be a game otherwise?

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:54.910
Geez!

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:57.660
You have to do your homework!

00:06:58.030 --> 00:07:01.410
I-It's not like I'm worried or anything.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:03.120
Fine.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:05.080
I'll do it if you say so.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:06.500
Hey, Konata.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:09.630
Why are the heroines in those games...

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:12.800
...always cute with great personalities yet unattached?

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:14.010
You can just pick and choose.

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:14.800
Beats me...

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.840
Maybe 'cause it wouldn't be a game otherwise?

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:18.850
Yo, Konata!

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:20.180
I'm here to play!

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:22.810
While checking on Yutaka.

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:24.270
Good evening, Cousin Yui.

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:25.520
Konata?

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:27.230
Your father's calling for you.

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:27.980
Okay.

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:31.480
Yutaka started on her homework so let me borrow some manga.

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:31.690
Er...

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:34.490
Don't you need to study, Konata?

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:36.110
Haven't you been playing this whole time?

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:36.740
No!

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:37.910
You've got it wrong!

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:40.740
You just have bad timing and enter whenever I'm taking a break!

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:44.790
But that just means you take a lot of breaks.

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:45.750
And so...

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:47.710
...I'm concerned about my image at home...

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:49.920
I try to stay at my desk...

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:51.420
...but I end up taking a break.

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:52.630
Honestly...

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:55.470
It's because you usually don't work hard.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:56.880
But well...

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:59.140
It's not like I don't understand how you feel.

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:01.600
You've had a similar experience?

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:02.680
Well...

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:05.520
If I pick up a book I really want to read during a break...

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:08.520
...I end up wanting to take another
break as soon as I start studying again.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:11.650
It's hard to put those down in the middle.

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:12.610
It's the same with manga.

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:14.900
You say you'll stop after one more volume...

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:18.450
...but then you end up reading dozens more.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:21.160
When you borrow the DVDs for a TV series you missed...

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:22.870
...you always have to watch one more episode.

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:25.830
But the follow-up tends to be trash.

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:27.040
I see.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:27.210
Director, about this doll...

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:28.170
Big Sister.

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:30.000
Can I change the channel?

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:30.790
Sure.

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:32.880
I wasn't really watching.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:35.300
Is there something you want to watch?

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:39.390
There's going to be a special on sweets from around the country.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:42.050
You love sweets, right?

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:43.430
I bet Kagami and Tsukasa will watch, too.

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:47.560
It's like the Hare Hare Dance of sweets!

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:48.850
That looks great!

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:50.150
With these shows...
It's like the Hare Hare Dance of sweets!

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:51.900
...even if you find something good...

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:54.940
...it ends up being sold somewhere far
away and you're left disappointed, right?

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:57.950
We live in Saitama, so Nagoya's kinda...

00:08:57.950 --> 00:08:59.570
That always happens...

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:01.160
...but I still end up watching.

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:02.030
Too bad.

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:06.330
Good morning, Yuki-chan.

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:07.790
Um, what's wrong?

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:10.540
I went to the dentist's yesterday.

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:12.290
You're still going?

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:14.500
I ran away halfway through...

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:18.720
Let me know if it hurts.

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:23.800
It'll be over soon.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.600
Something like that...

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:27.850
That's right!

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:29.440
They never stop!

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:30.940
It hurts to just hear about it!

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:32.980
We already have summer classes...

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:34.190
...but homework on top of that?

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:35.860
Screw that.

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:37.900
It's summer vacation.

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:40.860
It's not like you do it yourself anyway.

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:41.950
Besides...

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:44.160
...unlike grade school and middle school...

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.910
...we don't have independent projects or book reports.

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:48.620
Isn't this easier?

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:50.370
You just have to answer questions.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:53.380
We made crafts and posters, too.

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:54.670
With that stuff...

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:57.710
...you end up getting your parents' help.

00:09:57.710 --> 00:10:01.260
And then they get so into it that they finish it, right?

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:04.430
I won a prize off of that once.

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:06.260
With a poster or something.

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:07.600
I remember that.

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:09.140
I was like, "It's all thanks to you, Dad.

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:10.890
I think you're even cooler now!"

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:13.060
And Dad was all happy about it.

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:14.940
<i>Shouldn't a parent be mad about that?</i>

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:29.830
Buy at least five at once!

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:31.460
Whenever I see this commercial...

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:34.000
...I always get jealous.

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.170
When I was little...

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:37.960
...and read that fairy tale about a gingerbread house...

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:41.550
...I wanted to try eating all the candy I could!

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:43.050
I know what you mean...

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:45.800
...but when you actually get a lot of what you want...

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:47.810
...you tend to lose interest.

00:10:47.810 --> 00:10:49.100
Really...

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:50.310
Yeah.

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:51.930
It stinks the whole year.

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:54.020
So I was thinking...

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:55.860
About summer homework...

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:59.400
I'm always in trouble 'cause I plan
to do it in one go in the latter half.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:00.610
That came out of nowhere.

00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:02.650
And I didn't need you to tell me that.

00:11:02.650 --> 00:11:05.200
If I worked at it little by little...

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:07.490
...I might not have to scramble at the end.

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:09.540
You just realized that?

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:11.160
You're a third-year already.

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:13.250
Don't burn yourself out.

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:15.170
Which means I'll be coming over tomorrow so thanks.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:17.000
I'll bring a present.

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:19.500
So that's what you meant by little by little?

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:21.840
Are you going to come over all summer?

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:23.550
Probably every week.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:24.380
Shut up!

00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:27.640
Yo...

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:28.600
It's hot...

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:29.390
Yo.

00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:30.600
Sure is.

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:32.140
The A/C's on in my room.

00:11:33.230 --> 00:11:34.270
So comfortable!

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:36.480
You sure are making yourself at home...

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:38.020
It's like this every year.

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:41.690
Summer always passes without me wanting to do anything.

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:44.240
Before I know it, summer vacation's over.

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:46.200
Stop sounding so lazy.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:47.950
Set milestones this year...

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:49.740
...and get your homework done.

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:51.200
Well...

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:55.160
I plan on working hard before summer vacation begins every year.

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:56.170
Really?

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:57.370
In manga...

00:11:57.370 --> 00:12:00.130
You see the whole "I didn't do my homework!" gag used a lot...

00:12:00.130 --> 00:12:01.090
...this time of year.

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:01.880
That's true.

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:03.380
When you look at that...

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:07.260
...don't you think that in theory, you don't need to do it?

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:08.970
If that's what everybody else is doing...

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:10.390
Of course not!

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:10.890
Do it.

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:12.810
Besides, if you're gonna be like this, don't come to copy!

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:15.850
I'm thirsty.

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:18.310
I'll go get some barley tea.

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:19.270
Sis!

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:20.360
Sorry...

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:23.860
Could you also get the math problem set from my room?

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:24.570
Pretty please.

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:26.330
Yeah, yeah.

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:26.820
So hot!

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:29.070
You don't want to leave an air conditioned room...

00:12:29.070 --> 00:12:32.370
...so you ask someone else to do it when they leave...

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:35.910
...but nobody else wants to leave, huh?

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:38.040
In winter, you don't want to leave the kotatsu...

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:40.500
...so you ask someone else to do stuff for you when they get up.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:41.000
Hey.

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:42.130
Yo!

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:43.210
Sure is hot.
Yo.

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:44.170
Welcome.

00:12:44.170 --> 00:12:45.340
I brought ice cream.

00:12:45.340 --> 00:12:48.840
Take whichever one you want.

00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:51.640
Since I won't be much help with homework.

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:57.640
And the Marimokkori's eyes...

00:12:58.270 --> 00:13:00.150
<i>In these situations...</i>

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:04.020
<i>...why is it that you always want the ones other people chose?</i>

00:13:04.270 --> 00:13:07.740
I'm reading this manga about getting into Tokyo U.

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:08.990
That one, huh?

00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:10.160
When you read that...

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:13.120
...don't you start thinking that you
might have a chance to get into Tokyo U?

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:14.870
If you work hard like them!

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:16.540
You sure are simple.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:20.210
Even if that method could get you into Tokyo U...

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:23.880
You'd need friends who abandon their regular classes to join in...

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:26.130
Teachers who hold class like that...

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:27.840
Someone to take charge.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:30.880
And all kinds of other things for it to work, right?

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:32.010
You're right...

00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:34.140
It's not that easy...

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:35.390
<i>Too many people...</i>

00:13:35.390 --> 00:13:39.560
<i>...get influenced by manga or TV shows
and think they can change themselves.</i>

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:40.480
Well...

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:42.940
I plan on working hard and studying...

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:44.900
...but I always get sleepy.

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:48.400
Is there a good way to stay awake?

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:50.110
I think it's better to take a little nap...

00:13:50.110 --> 00:13:52.950
...than to force yourself to stay awake.

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:54.200
Oh, really?

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:56.740
I heard that before so I gave it a try...

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:59.160
But my little nap ended up being a lot longer...

00:13:59.160 --> 00:13:59.790
...yeah?

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:01.120
No willpower...

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:02.790
Hello!

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:03.250
Hello, Yutaka-chan.

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:04.540
Hello.

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:06.710
Um, do you have a minute?

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:08.130
What's up, Yu-chan?

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:10.340
You can ask us anything.

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:14.430
A friend from middle school apparently got a boyfriend...

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:18.810
...and she asked me what she should give him for his birthday.

00:14:18.810 --> 00:14:20.770
I have no idea...

00:14:22.850 --> 00:14:24.190
<i>What do I do...</i>

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:26.440
<i>It got really awkward...</i>

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:28.440
A-Anyway, Yu-chan...

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:31.150
They have web sites that discuss this stuff...

00:14:31.150 --> 00:14:33.030
...so you should take a look.

00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:35.280
There might be a thread about it.

00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:37.080
You can use my computer.

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:38.450
I-I'll do that.

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:40.540
I know about Tra** Man...

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:43.040
...but you can even ask questions about this stuff.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:45.960
It's pretty common these days.

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:47.920
Anything goes, huh?

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.250
That's right.

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:52.420
They probably have the answers for math problems, too.

00:14:52.420 --> 00:14:55.800
It makes me think how kids these days have it so easy.

00:14:56.090 --> 00:14:58.100
<i>As technology and the community advances...</i>

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:01.560
<i>...the users' mindset and willpower are getting worse.</i>

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:03.100
<i>Just look at her.</i>

00:15:07.770 --> 00:15:08.360
<i>Huh?</i>

00:15:08.360 --> 00:15:09.730
<i>That's odd...</i>

00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:11.990
<i>I'm just copying homework...</i>

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:13.200
<i>...but unlike usual...</i>

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:16.030
<i>...the presence of an audience creates this pride-like feeling...</i>

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:17.070
Oh, yeah.

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:19.030
What about the festival at your place?

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:20.410
What are you talking about?

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:21.410
It's already over.

00:15:21.410 --> 00:15:21.700
Wha—

00:15:21.700 --> 00:15:23.210
Same as last year.

00:15:23.210 --> 00:15:25.670
Why didn't you tell me?!

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:27.540
We have to study for exams.

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:30.380
If we told you, you'd definitely want to go.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:32.550
We didn't go either.

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:34.050
Doesn't have to be ours...

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:36.470
Just go to the one where you live.

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:37.550
Is it already over?

00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:39.050
Where I live...?

00:15:39.050 --> 00:15:40.760
Yeah, I wonder when that is...

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:41.930
Yeah...

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:44.430
Some people go to festivals in other places...

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:46.730
...but don't even care about the ones where they live.

00:15:46.730 --> 00:15:49.610
Are you the type who avoids friends from back home?

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:54.280
Even college applicants can't go on studying forever.

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:55.780
That's right...

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:58.450
There's going to be a fireworks display near my home tomorrow.

00:15:58.700 --> 00:15:59.740
That's it!

00:15:59.740 --> 00:16:02.490
Let's all go have fun for once!

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:03.910
Guess so.

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:05.370
We could use a break.

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:07.250
That's right.

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:10.840
There's going to be a fireworks display
near your home tomorrow, Minami-chan.

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:14.170
I'd like to see Japanese fireworks.

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:16.550
Then let's all go together, Minami.

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:17.590
Minami-chan.

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:18.800
Are you free tomorrow?

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:19.760
I'm good.

00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:21.720
Then it's decided, Minami.

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:24.140
Let's go, Iwasaki-san.

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:25.140
<i>Huh?</i>

00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:25.980
<i>Iwasaki-san?</i>

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:29.190
It's a pretty famous fireworks display...

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:29.860
...Mi—

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:30.730
Iwasaki-san.

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:35.400
<i>It's hard to change how you call
someone once you've gotten used to it.</i>

00:16:36.110 --> 00:16:39.660
But it's far away and famous so it'll be crowded, right?

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:41.370
Will you be okay, Yu-chan?

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:44.160
Weren't you sick a while back?

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:47.920
It's going to be hot tomorrow so should we wait for the next one?

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:51.170
You don't have to worry about me.

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:52.460
It happens all the time.

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:55.670
I'm the class health officer and I'll be coming...

00:16:55.670 --> 00:16:57.510
...so it'll be okay...

00:16:57.510 --> 00:16:58.470
...Yutaka.

00:16:59.090 --> 00:17:00.300
That's right.

00:17:00.300 --> 00:17:01.600
You're right.

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:03.850
Thanks, Minami-chan!

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:07.100
So we're going to see fireworks...

00:17:07.100 --> 00:17:09.140
...but otherwise it's college application and study time.

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:11.980
It sucks how I have less time to play.

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:13.820
'Cause Kagami and the others are all serious.

00:17:13.820 --> 00:17:15.570
Well, I can understand.

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:18.150
You should just do what you want.

00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:21.200
I used to drag Kanata around...

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:23.240
...and made lots of memories.

00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:24.490
I got in trouble...

00:17:24.490 --> 00:17:26.450
...but adolescence doesn't wait!

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:30.170
Then maybe I should get a boyfriend and make some memories.

00:17:31.330 --> 00:17:33.000
Absolutely not!

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:34.380
I won't accept a boyfriend!

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:35.130
Well, Dad...

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:37.010
You're not making sense.

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:37.800
That's right.

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:40.180
Wanna come watch fireworks with us, Yu-chan?

00:17:40.180 --> 00:17:42.220
Actually, I'm also going.

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:44.810
We're meeting up at Minami-chan's place.

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:45.850
Really...

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:48.810
We're leaving!

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:50.520
Have fun!

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:53.520
The train's here!

00:17:58.030 --> 00:17:59.570
You're late.

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:00.860
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:18:00.860 --> 00:18:03.530
Yutaka-chan came along.

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:04.410
Um...

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:05.410
Hey!

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:06.870
Hey! Hey! Hey!
Over here!

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:08.290
Hello.

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:08.830
Hey.

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:10.040
Hiya.

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:11.250
Patricia-san.

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:13.380
Are you also here for the fireworks?

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:14.920
You look good in a yukata.

00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:25.180
What the heck?!

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:34.690
Huh?

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:39.780
So Miyuki-san's neighbor was Minami-chan.

00:18:40.060 --> 00:18:41.740
What a coincidence.

00:18:41.740 --> 00:18:43.820
What a surprise.

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:45.070
Welcome.

00:18:45.070 --> 00:18:46.700
Here you go.

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:47.870
Thank you very much.

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:49.450
Oh?

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:50.870
Not enough?

00:18:51.640 --> 00:18:53.250
There should be enough...

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:54.210
Mom.

00:18:54.210 --> 00:18:56.630
Did you count yourself?

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:57.250
1.

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:57.840
2.

00:18:57.840 --> 00:18:58.380
3.

00:18:58.380 --> 00:18:59.050
4.

00:18:59.050 --> 00:18:59.590
5.

00:18:59.590 --> 00:19:00.050
6.

00:19:00.050 --> 00:19:00.550
7.

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:01.090
8.

00:19:01.090 --> 00:19:01.590
9.

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:03.010
My.

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:03.970
You're right.

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:05.930
<i>Now I get it.</i>

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:08.100
Thanks for having us!

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:10.600
So this is Minami-chan's house.

00:19:11.430 --> 00:19:13.190
Scary big dog...

00:19:13.190 --> 00:19:14.480
Don't worry.

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:16.100
It doesn't bark.

00:19:16.100 --> 00:19:17.480
And it's really friendly.

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:18.730
I see.

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:20.570
When they're big and friendly...

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:22.440
...it's actually kinda cute.

00:19:22.690 --> 00:19:23.610
Huh?

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:25.160
It's growling at me...

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:27.910
<i>Maybe she's the type who tends to get barked at.</i>

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:33.710
When I was little...

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:38.750
...I would wonder if fireworks were still round from the side.

00:19:38.750 --> 00:19:39.460
Huh?

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:41.210
So they don't look flat?

00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:42.050
Hey now...

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:45.760
They show firework displays on TV occassionally...

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:48.800
...but there's a better atmosphere when you watch the real thing.

00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:49.680
You're right.

00:19:49.970 --> 00:19:50.680
But you know...

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:52.560
I've been thinking...

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:54.480
Every time they launch a big one...

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:58.810
...and announce that this was
sponsored by some business or other...

00:19:58.810 --> 00:20:00.730
...doesn't that ruin the mood?

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:02.150
Th-That's true.

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:03.070
Huh?

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:03.820
Yu-chan.

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:05.860
You look a little pale.

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:07.360
I'm okay.

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:11.620
It's okay...

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:12.990
...so go watch.

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:13.540
But...

00:20:13.870 --> 00:20:15.210
I'll...

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:16.710
...stay here.

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:18.290
<i>Minami-chan.</i>

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:24.300
That was wonderful.

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:25.090
Yeah.

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:27.300
This is what summer's all about.

00:20:27.300 --> 00:20:28.010
But you know...

00:20:29.510 --> 00:20:33.270
It never ends up being a beautiful memory like in manga.

00:20:33.270 --> 00:20:35.060
I got bitten everywhere.

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:35.890
So itchy!

00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:38.690
They say that it itches more if you scratch.

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:42.860
And when you take off the yukata, it itches under the belt.

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:43.610
That's right.

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:45.360
Beautiful.

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:47.400
It really was.

00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:50.280
But sorry for causing you trouble.

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:52.450
There you are.

00:20:52.450 --> 00:20:53.410
Hey.

00:20:53.790 --> 00:20:56.580
Were you guys bitten by bugs, too?

00:20:57.580 --> 00:20:59.710
We didn't get bit at all.

00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:04.340
So some people are easily bitten and some aren't.

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:05.340
So lucky.

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:06.210
Nah.

00:21:06.210 --> 00:21:07.970
Maybe the mosquitos read the mood.

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:15.220
Good lucky!

00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:18.600
I'm your navigator, Akira Kogami!

00:21:18.850 --> 00:21:20.270
I'm the assistant...

00:21:20.270 --> 00:21:21.730
Daisuke Ono.

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:24.730
We're already on the twentieth episode of Lucky Channel!

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:26.900
You're not a crow today.

00:21:28.070 --> 00:21:29.950
You're not a dog today.

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:32.990
Then let's have a look at the live feed.

00:21:34.780 --> 00:21:37.290
I wonder where he is right now.

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:38.870
That Shiroishi-kun.

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:40.960
Mt. Fuji's so pretty!

00:21:41.330 --> 00:21:42.250
Whatever.

00:21:42.670 --> 00:21:44.000
Then bye-bee!

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:44.960
Bye-bee!

00:21:46.510 --> 00:21:47.590
Shiraishi-kun?

00:21:48.510 --> 00:21:49.220
Shiraishi-kun?!

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:24.290
Well, next time on Lucky Star:

00:23:24.290 --> 00:23:25.050
Misao here.

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:25.750
Ayano here.

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:26.670
Hey, Ayano.

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:28.340
Isn't Hiiragi so heartless?

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:30.550
She always runs off to the midget's class.

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:31.550
There, there.

00:23:31.550 --> 00:23:34.010
Does our love not reach Hiiragi?!

00:23:35.260 --> 00:23:36.640
Pandora's Box.

00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:38.520
Ayano's heartless, too...
